   "etymology": "A case of a loaned verb being suppleted by inherited forms.\nFrom Old Albanian vinj (“to come”), vjen (“he comes”), borrowed from Latin veniō. The past forms in erdh- are from Proto-Indo-European *h₁erǵʰ- and cognate with Ancient Greek ἔρχομαι (érkhomai).",
